fix(bin): align every inline consumer with the array-preserving returns

Tonight's comma-return fixes made list helpers hold their shape through
ASSIGNMENT - which is the one consumption the wrappers predate. An inline
@(...) around such a call now nests the array one level deep, and piping the
call directly passes the whole array as a single object; both shapes were
widespread because they were exactly right under the old unrolled returns.

Swept every caller of the array-preserving helpers (Get-FmFileLines,
Get-JqList, Get-ObligationName, Get-FmBackendHerdrJsonValue, Get-JArray,
Get-JList, Get-JSorted, Get-FmBackendCmuxJsonList): 29 sites in 17 files.
An inline wrap becomes a parenthesized expression (assignment semantics,
one unwrap), and a piped call is parenthesized first so the pipeline
enumerates elements rather than receiving the array whole.

Includes the two latent daemon sites the coverage suite flagged as
unreachable-today, so the next reachable path cannot revive the bug class.
Get-FmBusySourcesForHarness stays deliberately unrolled per its own header.

Probed all three shapes end-to-end under StrictMode: plain assignment,
parenthesized expression, parenthesized-then-piped - counts and elements
all correct. Lint over the 17 files adds zero findings.
